# =============================================================================
# smoke_test/.env.example  —  copy to smoke_test/.env and edit, OR just export
# these vars before running test.sh. Every value has a sensible default, so the
# file is OPTIONAL; you only need it to point at your deployment.
#
#   cp smoke_test/.env.example smoke_test/.env
#   vim smoke_test/.env
# =============================================================================

# --- target (service under test) --------------------------------------------
# Base URL of the PROFILE service. On the app box it's published on host port
# 10002 (10002 -> container 8000).
#   on the box:        http://127.0.0.1:10002
#   from a laptop:     http://<deploy-host>:10002
#   via API gateway:   http://<deploy-host>:10015   (gateway rewrites /api/v1/profile/*)
PROFILE_URL=http://<deploy-host>:10002

# --- peers needed to TEST profile (taken from env, per the platform rule) ----
# Profile is downstream: its protected routes need a real RS256 token, and a
# profile row only exists after profile consumes auth's UserCreated event. So
# the harness mints users/tokens from AUTH and recovers OTP codes from SUPPORT.
# Profile itself makes NO HTTP call to auth (it verifies the JWT offline with
# auth's public key) — these URLs are for the TEST, not the service.
AUTH_URL=http://<deploy-host>:10001
SUPPORT_URL=http://<deploy-host>:10099

# The seeded platform admin phone (auth config DEFAULT_ADMIN_PHONE). The harness
# logs in as admin to exercise GET /admin/profiles/{user_id}.
ADMIN_PHONE=01700000000

# --- OTP recovery fallback (only if SUPPORT_URL is unreachable) --------------
# OTP is enabled on auth; /verify needs the real 6-digit code. Preferred source
# is the SUPPORT service above. Fallbacks: local `docker logs` (on the box) or
# over SSH from a laptop.
AUTH_CONTAINER=dokandar_auth_service_dev
# AUTH_SSH=ubuntu@<deploy-host>
# AUTH_SSH_KEY=/home/jakir/Desktop/DevOps/mumbai-key.pem

# --- admin OTP rate-limit reset (best-effort) --------------------------------
# The seeded admin phone is reused every run; auth's OTP_RATE_PER_HOUR (=5)
# would throttle admin login after a few reruns. The harness clears the admin's
# per-phone OTP rate key at startup if it can reach auth's Redis (directly, or
# via the auth container over SSH). Override the redis URL here if needed.
# REDIS_RESET_URL=redis://:<password>@<infra-host>:6379/0

# --- harness knobs -----------------------------------------------------------
# per-request curl timeout, seconds (keep comments on their OWN line, not inline)
TIMEOUT=15
# /health fans out to kafka/mongo/apm so it gets a longer timeout
HEALTH_TIMEOUT=30
# seconds to wait for C1's profile to materialize via the UserCreated Kafka event
MATERIALIZE_TIMEOUT=40
# OUTPUT_DIR=./smoke_test/out
# NO_COLOR=1

# =============================================================================
# Cross-service note (per the platform convention of taking peer endpoints from
# env): profile PRODUCES dokandar.profile.changed / dokandar.address.changed and
# CONSUMES dokandar.user.{created,updated} + dokandar.kyc.* over Kafka, and it
# EXPOSES a gRPC ProfileQuery (:20002). It does not make synchronous HTTP calls
# to peers (Media is gRPC, diagnostic-only on /health). The only peers this TEST
# needs are AUTH (mint tokens) and SUPPORT (read OTP codes). The fleet-standard
# digit-prefixed vars below are accepted-but-ignored (not valid shell idents).
# =============================================================================
# 01_AUTH_HOST=<infra-host>
# 01_AUTH_PORT=10001
# 02_PROFILE_HOST=<infra-host>
# 02_PROFILE_PORT=10002
